{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Hārita (1st)","html":"<article id='thag1.29'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.29 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.29 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Hāritattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hārita (1st) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Samunnamayamattānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Straighten yourself, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>usukārova tejanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a fletcher an arrow. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cittaṁ ujuṁ karitvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When your mind is upright, Hārita, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>avijjaṁ bhinda hāritā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>break ignorance to bits! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Hārito thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
